  "title": "Plum Jelly",
  "description": "This easy plum jelly recipe combines fresh, juicy plums with sugar and water for a simple, sweet homemade preserve you can enjoy year-round.",
  "authors": [
    "Shady Acres Cooking"
  ],
  "date_published": "2020-06-19T00:40:33-04:00",
  "date_modified": "2025-12-10T16:38:23-05:00",
  "prep_time": "PT15M",
  "cook_time": "PT45M",
  "total_time": "PT60M",
  "yield": [
    "5",
    "5 (½-pint) jars"
  ],
  "categories": [
    "Jam / Jelly"
  ],
  "cuisines": [
    "American"
  ],
  "regions": [
    "American"
  ],
  "breadcrumbs": [],
  "keywords": [],
  "ingredients": [
    "2.5 pounds fresh plums, pitted and halved",
    "4 cups white sugar",
    "1 cup water"
  ],
  "steps": [
    {
      "text": "Gather all ingredients.",
      "section": null,
      "name": null,
      "url": null,
      "image_sources": [
        "https://www.allrecipes.com/thmb/v0t7MKdPiRij_BXHNlNLWbL79Nk=/1500x0/filters:no_upscale():max_bytes(150000):strip_icc()/ALR-275563-plum-jelly-VAT-step-01-4c648d8146b149c3b099cc577eb9d11d.jpg"
      ],
      "image": "assets/images/275563/step_01.webp"
    },
    {
      "text": "Combine plums, sugar, and water in a large pot over medium-high heat. Bring to a boil, stirring until sugar dissolves. Lower heat to medium and cook, stirring occasionally to prevent sticking, until mixture has thickened to desired consistency, 30 to 40 minutes.",
      "section": null,
      "name": null,
      "url": null,
      "image_sources": [
        "https://www.allrecipes.com/thmb/GgsyB8mlBrFn7eB43Mv9aC2otT8=/1500x0/filters:no_upscale():max_bytes(150000):strip_icc()/ALR-275563-plum-jelly-VAT-step-02-2c31678f0df54907a5a98bcfe3613e59.jpg"
      ],
      "image": "assets/images/275563/step_02.webp"
    },
    {
      "text": "Meanwhile, inspect five (½-pint) jars for cracks and rings for rust, discarding any defective ones. Immerse in simmering water until jelly is ready. Wash new, unused lids and rings in warm soapy water.",
      "section": null,
      "name": null,
      "url": null,
      "image_sources": [
        "https://www.allrecipes.com/thmb/N897C-iKs-vAqEgWupP1ZhsabCQ=/1500x0/filters:no_upscale():max_bytes(150000):strip_icc()/ALR-275563-plum-jelly-VAT-step-03-cd26564b44864125bb2b81c1c90b2688.jpg"
      ],
      "image": "assets/images/275563/step_03.webp"
    },
    {
      "text": "Remove jelly from heat and skim off any heavy foam. Ladle hot jelly into hot, sterilized jars, filling to within 1/2 inch of the top. Run a clean knife or thin spatula around the insides of the jars to remove any air bubbles. Wipe rims with a moist paper towel to remove any residue. Top with lids and screw rings on tightly.",
      "section": null,
      "name": null,
      "url": null,
      "image_sources": [
        "https://www.allrecipes.com/thmb/ljXMsxXki5Mdo2dPuOPczExmuGo=/1500x0/filters:no_upscale():max_bytes(150000):strip_icc()/ALR-275563-plum-jelly-VAT-step-04-1bb34af5dd9540228344f206075be2d5.jpg"
      ],
      "image": "assets/images/275563/step_04.webp"
    },
    {
      "text": "Place a rack in the bottom of a large stockpot and fill halfway with water. Bring to a boil and lower jars 2 inches apart into the boiling water using a holder.",
      "section": null,
      "name": null,
      "url": null,
      "image_sources": [
        "https://www.allrecipes.com/thmb/3lECHUHtqo9jE1FKkH-DCUI7iyc=/1500x0/filters:no_upscale():max_bytes(150000):strip_icc()/ALR-275563-plum-jelly-VAT-step-05-39afd7fa2b6b4c0cbc8a3c5348ba3b1f.jpg"
      ],
      "image": "assets/images/275563/step_05.webp"
    },
    {
      "text": "Pour in more boiling water to cover jars by at least 1 inch. Bring to a rolling boil, cover, and process for 15 minutes.",
      "section": null,
      "name": null,
      "url": null,
      "image_sources": [
        "https://www.allrecipes.com/thmb/-YgG3v6EqBloRAyBNPOMp7oLbgE=/1500x0/filters:no_upscale():max_bytes(150000):strip_icc()/ALR-275563-plum-jelly-VAT-step-06-f8639da9cf194228909f7d66895acf06.jpg"
      ],
      "image": "assets/images/275563/step_06.webp"
    },
    {
      "text": "Remove the jars from the stockpot and let rest, several inches apart, for 12 to 24 hours. Store in a cool, dark area.",
      "section": null,
      "name": null,
      "url": null,
      "image_sources": [
        "https://www.allrecipes.com/thmb/FKRg2WkKUuEOs7cBKhnCEFFefOA=/1500x0/filters:no_upscale():max_bytes(150000):strip_icc()/ALR-275563-plum-jelly-VAT-step-07-c34428651f5347baaea4356c927ee56c.jpg"
      ],
      "image": "assets/images/275563/step_07.webp"
    }
  ],
